10. Required Changes for Compatibility\
\pard\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs22 \cf3 Based on the flight 4 analysis, the following items need verification and possible changes:
\fs32 \cf2 \
\pard\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 10.1 Verify state_to_telem_id() Mapping\
\pard\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs22 \cf3 If the altimeter firmware has added internal flight states beyond the original four (PAD_IDLE, ASCENT, DESCENT, LANDED), the 
\f3\fs20 state_to_telem_id()
\f0\fs22  function must map ALL internal states to the 4 valid $PYRO codes (0-3), as described in Section 3. Any unmapped state that leaks to the serial output will break the ground station display.
\fs26 \cf2 \
\pard\sa120\partightenfactor0

\fs22 \cf3 Mapping rules for new internal states:
\fs26 \cf2 \
\pard\tx360\tx720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f6\b0\fs20\fsmilli10000 \cf3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Any boot/calibration state \uc0\u8594  Do not send telemetry (or send state_id 0)
\f6\fs20 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Any ascending/coasting state \uc0\u8594  state_id 1 (ASCENT), with thrust flag set appropriately
\f6\fs20 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Any descending state (drogue, main, ballistic) \uc0\u8594  state_id 2 (DESCENT)
\f6\fs20 \
