\fs22 \cf3 Events marked Both can be triggered by either an event sentence or a flag transition. The tracker deduplicates: if a $PYRO_APO sentence fires the APOGEE event, the subsequent FLAG_APOGEE transition is suppressed (and vice versa). The altimeter should send event sentences for the most accurate timing; the flag-based detection serves as a fallback.
\fs32 \cf2 \
\pard\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 13. Quick Reference for Altimeter Developers\
\pard\tx360\tx720\li720\fi-720\sa80\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f6\b0\fs20\fsmilli10000 \cf3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone The $PYRO state_id field must be 0, 1, 2, or 3. No other values.
\f6\fs20 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	2.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Thrust flag = 1 during motor burn, 0 otherwise. This creates the BOOST vs COAST distinction.
\f6\fs20 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone All descent phases (drogue, main, ballistic) = state_id 2.
\f6\fs20 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	4.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Landed = state_id 3. The ground station auto-completes after 5 minutes of continuous state_id 3.
\f6\fs20 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	5.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Emit $PYRO_APO, $PYRO_FIRE, $PYRO_LAND event sentences at the appropriate moments.
\f6\fs20 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	6.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Flags bits 0-5 must be maintained correctly. The tracker watches for 0\uc0\u8594 1 transitions.
\f6\fs20 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	7.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone telem_format must default to 0 (NMEA). The tracker cannot parse JSON.
\f6\fs20 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs20\fsmilli10000 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	8.	}
\f2\fs22 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 10 Hz during ASCENT and DESCENT, 1 Hz during PAD and LANDED.}